            <ArticleTitle>[Results of computerized processing of myocardial 99mTc-pyrophosphate scans in ischemic heart disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>23-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Myocardial scintigraphy was carried out in 105 coronary heart disease patients using 99mTc -pyrophosphate. Twenty-nine of these patients suffered from acute myocardial infarction. The scintigrams were analyzed with the aid of original &quot; MAREA &quot; programmes devised for the diagnosis of acute myocardial infarction. The results obtained suggest the possibility of using this method of the scintigram processing for assessing the severity and predicting the course of coronary heart disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
